---
import WikiHowLayout from '../../layouts/WikiHowLayout.astro';

const title = "The Hidden Math: Unlocking the Golden Ratio in Modern Design";
const author = "Elena Rostova";
const updatedAt = "July 14, 2026";
const views = "42,010";
const category = "Web Design";
---
<WikiHowLayout title={title} author={author} updatedAt={updatedAt} views={views} category={category}>
  
  <p>Why do certain websites look inherently beautiful while others feel "off"? The answer lies in a 2,000-year-old mathematical sequence known as the Golden Ratio. Here is how to apply it to your designs.</p>
  
  <img src="/images/blog/golden-ratio.png" alt="Golden ratio overlay" class="wikihow-image" />

  <h2><span class="wikihow-step-num">1</span> Understand Phi (1.618).</h2>
  <p>The Golden Ratio is a mathematical constant found throughout nature. In geometry, a Golden Rectangle is one whose side lengths are in the ratio of 1:1.618. Human psychology is deeply wired to find this proportion aesthetically pleasing.</p>

  <h2><span class="wikihow-step-num">2</span> Scale Typography Mathematically.</h2>
  <p>Top-tier UI designers do not guess font sizes. If your body text is 16px, multiply it by 1.618 to get your Header size (approx 26px). Multiply that by 1.618 for your Hero Title (approx 42px). This creates perfect typographic hierarchy.</p>

  <h2><span class="wikihow-step-num">3</span> Build Golden Layout Grids.</h2>
  <p>Divide your total screen width by 1.618. For a standard 1920px wide screen, the main content area should be roughly 1187px wide, leaving exactly enough room for a perfectly proportioned sidebar.</p>

  <h2><span class="wikihow-step-num">4</span> Validate with Digital Rulers.</h2>
  <p>You don't need to guess if your layout is perfect. Use an <a href="/ruler" class="text-[#9eb96e] font-bold hover:underline">Online Digital Ruler</a> to measure the exact pixel widths of your columns on the screen and ensure they conform to the 1.618 ratio.</p>

</WikiHowLayout>
